  Q6-06 0.52 (noul 0.58 score 0.45) vs CL: The Chicxulub crater is dated to within 30,000 years of the extinction.
  Q1-08 0.38 (noul 0.43 score 0.32) vs BR: The observed acceleration is fitted slightly better by a constant dark energy than by a growing one.
  Q1-05 0.33 (noul 0.36 score 0.30) vs BR: Heat death is the outcome predicted by the simplest model that fits all current cosmological data (Lambda-CDM).
  Q5-09 0.31 (noul 0.35 score 0.28) vs PY: Go produces a single static binary, which makes deployment simpler than with Python.
  Q3-07 0.29 (noul 0.35 score 0.22) vs EQ: The last letters from Ugarit describe enemy ships attacking the coast.
  Q5-07 0.29 (noul 0.41 score 0.16) vs JV: Python lets small teams ship a first version faster than Java does.
  Q1-06 0.27 (noul 0.27 score 0.26) vs BR: Big Rip models need more free parameters than a cosmological constant, so Occam's razor favours heat death.
  Q3-06 0.26 (noul 0.33 score 0.19) vs EQ: Evidence for the drought is stronger and more widespread than evidence for an earthquake storm.
